  "worked_solution": "First, we simplify the expression by distributing the subtraction over the matrices in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+B-(C+B) & =A+B-C-B \\\\  & =A+\\cancel{B}-C-\\cancel{B} \\\\  & =A-C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are left with a single subtraction. So, we subtract the corresponding entries of the two matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-C & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}8 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2-8 & -5-(-2) \\\\ 7-(-4) & 0-1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -3 \\\\ 11 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
